title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-ticklers/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A tickler is a reminder for a HyperGSD action that you can set for a specific date.

When the date arrives, an alert will appear that links to the action you set the tickler on.

You can optionally set the tickler to repeat every //n// days.

The plugin also provides the [[GSD/Ticklers]] dashboard for an overview of upcoming actions of interest on certain days.

! The tickler check

The check runs automatically when the wiki loads, at <samp>hh:00</samp> every hour and at local midnight, and only in an open browser session. There is no server-side timer when used as part of a server.

A tiddler that has a tickler with today's date will raise a //Tickler due// alert banner.

Repeating ticklers advance by whole intervals from the fired date (the weekday is preserved), and a completed repeating tickler still raises one banner on each due date. The date is never removed by triggering the alert. An overdue tickler stays in the [[GSD/Ticklers]] dashboard until handled and a tickler missed while the wiki was closed raises a //Tickler overdue// banner at the first check after (an overdue one-shot re-raises once a day until handled; a repeating one alerts once per missed occurrence).
''THIS IS ALL HARD TO READ''

Completing the action dismisses the alert; pressing the button to increment will update with a new due dat and dismiss the alert.

The shift buttons are data-only tag-list tiddlers rendered by the shared `$hgsd.tickler-shift` widget: tag `$:/tags/hypergsd/Ticklers/Shift` for the panel set, add `$:/tags/hypergsd/Ticklers/Alert` to also appear on the banner; fields `days`, `label`, `tooltip` (plain text or `<<lingo>>` keys) and an optional `class`. The widget takes `target-tiddler`, `base-date` (panel = stored date, alert = now), `days`, `label`, `tooltip`, `class`, `after-shift-actions` and `lingo-base`, and is equally usable standalone with explicit parameters.

This plugin ships with separate alert banner and panel/modal tiddlers. They can be turned on/off in Settings → HyperGSD → Ticklers.

! Fields

|Field |Meaning |h
|`gsd_tickler_date` |When the tickler fires, as a TiddlyWiki UTC date string at midnight |
|`gsd_tickler_date_history` |Chronological list of every date the tickler has carried. The last entry is always the current date. It is not displayed anywhere as part of this plugin. |
|`gsd_tickler_repeat_days` |Repeat interval in days. If empty, the alert will only trigger on the due date. |

A repeating tickler that is marked complete, //stays// complete. Its alert still returns on each due date, once per cycle. -- WHATS A CYCLE

